> With hard-wired limited options?

The options are only as hard-wired as the class-writer wants them to
be.  If you say:

   \DeclareOption*{\myoptionparser}

then your option parser can do what it likes with \CurrentOption.  For
example:

\def\myoptionparser{%
   \expandafter\@myoptionparser\CurrentOption==\@myoptionparser%
}

\def\@myoptionparser#1=#2=#3\@myoptionparser{%
   ... do something with keyword #1 = value #2 ...
}

And voila, you've got keyword=value options.

Whether you'd actually *want* keyword=value options is another
matter...

Alan.

